@@name
performance
@@description
Improve the performance characteristic named in the user request, proven by measurement, without changing results.
@@requirements
    - Measure a baseline before changing anything, with a repeatable command or benchmark
    - Profile to find where the time or memory actually goes before optimising
    - Report before and after numbers from the same measurement
@@approach
    Before optimising, reason through:
    - What the profile shows as the dominant cost
    - Which change addresses that cost with the least added complexity
    Commit to the change and re-measure.
@@verification
    - Re-run the baseline measurement and confirm the improvement, with identical output
@@constraints
    - Outputs and behaviour stay identical; tests keep passing
    - No micro-optimisations that do not show up in the measurement
@@out-of-scope
    - Optimising code paths the profile does not implicate
